{"cluster_id": "C-3400", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B002-098", "B035-065"], "canonical_claim": "No registered namespace may be a path-prefix of another namespace, because shard discovery uses prefix LIST and nesting would mix their keys.; CA namespaces must not nest because GC enumerates by prefix LIST; the two verbatim-file locations are loose files under `roots/<server>/<path>` and files under `@cas@/_files/`, while the `_disk` magic namespace was eliminated.", "issue_ids": ["B181"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#path-mapping", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#blocking-gaps", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#gap-fill"]}
