{"cluster_id": "C-3407", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B004-040", "B038-009", "B040-152"], "canonical_claim": "CAS metadata objects use a text envelope whose header is `{\"type\":\"cas_<object>\",\"v\":N}`; `.zst` keys denote kinds whose policy always compresses.; Every persisted CAS object is a text file with header `{\"type\":\"cas_<object>\",\"v\":N}`, a body consisting of JSON, sorted NDJSON, or a raw payload zone, and an optional `{\"n\":\u2026}` trailer.; Every v3 CAS object uses a header line, a body, and an optional trailer line; type identifies the object and v is the only compatibility version", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#envelope", "docs/superpowers/cas/codecs_proposal_v3.md#one-file-shape", "src/Disks/DiskObjectStorage/MetadataStorages/ContentAddressed/Formats/README.md#L1-L6"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3408", "topic": "root shard incarnation", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B004-087", "B004-102"], "canonical_claim": "The planned `mutateShard` birth path stamps `RootShard::incarnation` only when creating a fresh object and leaves the incarnation immutable when mutating an existing object. Additionally, `RootShard::incarnation` is stamped once at create-if-absent, never mutated by later writes, and is encoded in the root-shard protobuf; missing incarnation data where required is fail-closed because CA has no compatibility scaffolding.", "issue_ids": ["D1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-01-cas-shard-incarnation-and-registry-removal.md#L100-L149", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-01-cas-shard-incarnation-and-registry-removal-design.md#incarnation"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3409", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B008-012"], "canonical_claim": "`PartFolderView` filters mutable names beginning with `.ca_` from user-visible file and directory answers.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase1.md#task-5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3410", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B008-013"], "canonical_claim": "`PartFolderView::projectionDirPrefix` recognizes a projection directory when its last path component ends in `.proj` or `.tmp_proj`, returning the routed file path with a trailing slash; other paths return no prefix.", "issue_ids": ["B64"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase1.md#task-5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3411", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B009-076"], "canonical_claim": "The v3 meta key is blobs/xx/<hash>.meta, while the body remains blobs/xx/<hash>; GC writes condemned before deletion, clears it on spare, and deletes it after the body.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-09-cas-writer-gc-simplification-design.md##meta-layout"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3412", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B010-003"], "canonical_claim": "In the raw-body design, a blob body is stored at `blobs/xx/<hash>` as a raw payload written once with `PUT If-None-Match`, while its meta is stored at `blobs/xx/<hash>.meta` and is the only conditionally-operated object.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L10-L17"]}
