{"cluster_id": "C-3414", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B010-057"], "canonical_claim": "Ref-log objects use `cas/refs/<archive-ns@cas@>/_log/<incarnation>/<seq>/...`, where `seq` is a fixed-width 16-digit lower-case hexadecimal sequence beginning at one.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#ref-log-paths"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3415", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B010-058"], "canonical_claim": "Inline ref-log records use `_log/<incarnation>/<seq>/precommit/<manifest_ref_suffix>/<ref...>`, `_log/<incarnation>/<seq>/abandon/<manifest_ref_suffix>/<ref...>`, `_log/<incarnation>/<seq>/drop/<manifest_ref_suffix>/<ref...>`, `_log/<incarnation>/<seq>/clear-precommits-before/<writer_epoch>`, or `_log/<incarnation>/<seq>/remove-namespace`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#ref-log-paths"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3416", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B010-074"], "canonical_claim": "Phase 1 GC stores one complete canonical ref base under `gc/gen/<generation>/attempt/<attempt>/ref-base/<run_ordinal>.run`, and the fold seal names each exact `RunRef`, checksum, minimum key, and maximum key.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#gc-owned-fold-format"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3417", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B011-006"], "canonical_claim": "A `kCondemned` run row has type byte `0x02`, uses the sentinel key `(blob_hash, source_id = 0)`, and encodes flags with bit 0 for `delete_pending`, `token_type`, `condemn_round`, `size`, `token_len`, and token bytes.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#run-rows"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3418", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B011-009", "B011-055"], "canonical_claim": "The sentinel key with `source_id = 0` sorts before all real edges of the same blob, allowing the merge cursor to settle condemned state at blob close-out.; Schema-3 settlement keys are ordered as `(algo, digest, source_id)` because the algorithm byte precedes variable-width digest bytes; the zero-source sentinel sorts first within each blob group.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#run-rows", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools-design.md#gc-keys"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3419", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B011-012"], "canonical_claim": "Source-edge run headers use `key_schema = 1` for `RunKind::SourceEdge`, and every consumer must validate `kind == SourceEdge`, `key_schema == 1`, and row payload lengths through a typed open path.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#run-rows"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3420", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B011-081"], "canonical_claim": "The canonical `RefTxnId` rendering is two lower-case fixed-width 16-digit hexadecimal numbers separated by `-`, such as `0000000000000007-000000000000008e`; noncanonical forms are rejected.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#ordered-ref-transaction-identifier"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3421", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B011-091"], "canonical_claim": "Phase 1 uses exactly one body-only log encoding at `_log/<txn-id>`; ref names are not encoded in object keys and invalid relative paths, including empty, `.`, `..`, repeated separators, NUL bytes, and noncanonical escaping, are rejected.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#one-log-encoding"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3422", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B011-053", "B011-151"], "canonical_claim": "The mixed-algorithm implementation deletes `kSourceEdgeKeySchema128`, `kSourceEdgeKeySchemaSha256`, `sourceEdgeDigestLen`, and `sourceEdgeKeySchemaFor`; there is one self-describing schema-3 settlement key codec.; Settlement uses source-edge key schema 3 with key bytes `algo(u8) ++ digest[blobHashLenFor(algo)] ++ source_id(16 BE)`, producing 33-byte keys for 16-byte algorithms and 49-byte keys for SHA-256.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools.md#task-3", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools-design.md#gc-keys"]}
