{"cluster_id": "C-3424", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B015-080"], "canonical_claim": "`txn_version.txt` is the only genuinely in-place-mutable per-part file identified by the all-tree design.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-all-tree-part-files-design.md#findings"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3425", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B015-081"], "canonical_claim": "`uuid.txt` is write-once and checksummed, so changing it in place would break `CHECK TABLE` even on vanilla storage.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-all-tree-part-files-design.md#findings"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3426", "topic": "all-tree part files", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B015-079", "B016-001", "B016-013", "B043-029"], "canonical_claim": "All per-part files are designed to become ordinary manifest tree entries, making the per-ref mutable-file set empty. Additionally, The CAS all-tree model makes `uuid.txt`, `metadata_version.txt`, and `txn_version.txt` ordinary manifest tree entries, with no mutable per-part files; standalone writes and removes on committed parts use an audited manifest repoint. Additionally, Writes of `uuid.txt`, `metadata_version.txt`, and `txn_version.txt` follow the normal content-entry path: they are included in the initial manifest during part build and trigger a manifest repoint when written on a committed part. Additionally, All part files, including previously mutable files, are content-addressed; committed-part repoint and an MVCC atomic-write short-circuit handle updates.", "issue_ids": ["B123"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/how-we-got-here.md#turn-maturation", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-all-tree-part-files.md#plan", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-all-tree-part-files.md#task-6", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-all-tree-part-files-design.md#decisions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3427", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B016-012"], "canonical_claim": "`supportsAtomicFileWrites()` defaults to false on `IDataPartStorage` and `IMetadataStorage`; `ContentAddressedMetadataStorage` returns true, `DataPartStorageOnDiskBase` delegates the capability, and `VersionMetadataOnDisk::storeInfoToDataPartStorage` uses one finalized and synced write instead of the tmp-plus-replace sequence when it is true.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-all-tree-part-files.md#task-5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3428", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B016-057", "B039-111"], "canonical_claim": "`PoolMeta` is authoritative on reopen: `pool_id`, `blob_header_len`, `min_reader_generation`, and the admitted hash-algorithm list come from `_pool_meta`, while creation arguments apply only at first creation.; `Cas::PoolMeta` owns immutable pool identity `pool_id` and constants `root_shards` and `blob_header_len`, and is authoritative on pool reopen.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["cas_disks_architecture_analysis.md#2-current-feature-map", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase2-control-plane.md#task2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3429", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B017-010", "B040-159"], "canonical_claim": "`cas_ref_log` keys use the `Always` `.zst` suffix, while `cas_ref_snap` keys replace their `.proto` suffix with `.zst`.; Tiny control types cas_pool_meta, cas_gc_state, cas_gc_hb, cas_owner, cas_epoch, cas_mount_lease, and cas_blob_meta are raw bare JSON, while cas_ref_snap, cas_ref_log, and cas_gc_outcomes are Always-compressed .zst controls", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/codecs_proposal_v3.md#control-plane", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase3-refsnaplog.md#cruxes"]}

